cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Advanced RAG — Hands On"
message: "If you use this material in teaching or research, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "the maintainers"
    website: "https://github.com/akash-coded/nanorag"
repository-code: "https://github.com/akash-coded/nanorag"
abstract: >-
  A runnable retrieval, RAG and evaluation curriculum. Ten Jupyter notebooks and a Python
  toolkit implementing lexical and dense retrieval, approximate nearest-neighbour search,
  hybrid fusion, learned reranking, context packing, LLM-judge calibration, token economics
  and agentic search — running entirely in memory with deterministic, reproducible
  measurements and an evaluation gate in CI.
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - information retrieval
  - evaluation
  - BM25
  - reranking
  - LLM-as-a-judge
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-31"
